## 3. Model Specification

### Architecture and tensor shapes

Defaults come directly from `include/config.h:22`.

| Quantity | Value |
|---|---:|
| Vocabulary `V` | 4096 |
| Maximum context `Tm` | 256 |
| Transformer layers `L` | 6 |
| Attention heads `NH` | 4 |
| Hidden channels `C` | 128 |
| Head dimension `C/NH` | 32 |
| MLP hidden dimension `4C` | 512 |
| Parameters | 1,746,944 |

The parameter-count formula derived from `param_sizes` is:

```text
V*C + Tm*C + L*(12*C*C + 13*C) + 2*C
```

See `src/model.c:57`.

This is a **GPT-2-style sequential pre-LayerNorm transformer**. The reference to “Pythia-14M shape” describes selected dimensions; this implementation is not a 14-million-parameter Pythia model. The documentation explicitly distinguishes the architectures at `docs/01-model.md:126`.

Inputs are integer token IDs `[B,T]`. Outputs are logits `[B,T,V]`, with probabilities and per-token losses produced when targets are supplied. Hidden activations use row-major `[B,T,C]`; linear weights use `[C_out,C_in]`. See `include/ops.h:3`.

For token position `t`:

```text
x_t = W_token[id_t] + W_position[t]
```

Each block computes:

```text
u = x + AttProj(Attention(QKV(LN1(x))))
y = u + FCProj(GELU(FC(LN2(u))))
```

After all blocks:

```text
z = LNf(y) @ W_token^T
```

There is no separate output weight matrix or output bias. There is no implemented dropout, rotary positional embedding, padding mask, or story-boundary attention mask. The actual block wiring is at `src/model.c:298`.

### Attention, normalization, and activation

Attention uses:

```text
a[t,j] = softmax over j <= t of (dot(q_t, k_j) / sqrt(C/NH))
o_t = sum over j <= t of a[t,j] * v_j
```

Future positions receive zero probability. QKV is packed `[B,T,3C]` as `[Q | K | V]`; attention probabilities are `[B,NH,T,T]`. See `src/cpu/attention.c:33`.

LayerNorm uses population variance over channels and epsilon `1e-5`. See `src/cpu/layernorm.c:12`.

GELU uses the tanh approximation:

```text
GELU(x) = 0.5*x*(1 + tanh(sqrt(2/pi)*(x + 0.044715*x^3)))
```

See `src/cpu/gelu.c:18`.

### Loss and gradient normalization

For supplied next-token targets:

```text
loss = -sum_i log(p[i, target[i]]) / (B*T)
dlogits[i,v] = (p[i,v] - indicator(v == target[i])) / (B*T)
```

Every position contributes equally. There is no ignore index or masked-token denominator. Targets are accepted as supplied; the model does **not** shift inputs itself.

See `src/cpu/crossentropy.c:22` and `src/cpu/crossentropy.c:54`.

### Initialization and reproducibility

`init_params` implements:

- Token embeddings, positional embeddings, QKV, and MLP expansion weights: normal distribution with standard deviation `0.02`.
- Attention and MLP residual projections: standard deviation `0.02 / sqrt(2L)`.
- LayerNorm scales: one.
- Biases: zero from zero-initialized allocation.

See `src/model.c:181`.

The seed is passed explicitly to `gpt_build`. The RNG is global-state xorshift64*, with Box–Muller normal sampling. Seed zero maps to a fixed nonzero constant. This supports repeatable initialization in a fixed environment, but floating-point math libraries and compiler behavior prevent asserting universal bitwise equivalence. See `src/utils.c:51`.

### Dataset: present behavior versus planned format

**Implemented preprocessing:**

- Reads up to 25 MiB from `data/TinyStories-train.txt`.
- Splits on `<|endoftext|>`.
- Trims leading/trailing whitespace.
- Keeps printable ASCII plus newline.
- Tokenizes words, numbers, punctuation, spaces, and newlines.
- Counts enough whole stories to reach approximately five million tokens.
- Assigns frequent-word IDs, reserving `0` for EOS and `1` for unknown.
- Prints statistics and frees everything.

It does **not** encode the corpus or write binary files. See `tools/prep_data.c:20`, `tools/prep_data.c:123`, and `tools/prep_data.c:226`.

**Planned format:** BPE vocabulary of 4096 entries, EOS `0`, base characters `1–96`, learned merges, no unknown token, `uint16` training/validation token streams. See `docs/01-model.md:5`.

The binary header, byte order, vocabulary serialization, split policy, and loader ownership contract are unspecified.

